Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 09:13:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 41/57] fix: DOF 3.0 lens model - physical CoC texture, real
 splat cap, 121 jittered taps, one-pixel polygon edge

Four defects in the %_RT_SAMPLE2 lens-model path, all of which made the sprite and the gather
disagree on screen. The stock permutation is untouched throughout.

1. The CoC texture was clamped to the GATHER's cap. LensModelCoC is called from the downscale,
   so the CoC target and everything built from it - the tile min/max pass, the layer alphas and
   above all the SPRITE's size - never saw anything past the kernel's reach; the splat cap was
   dead code and the sprite could not grow past the gather's disc, which is the one thing it
   exists to do. The texture now carries the PHYSICAL circle of confusion, clamped only to the
   splat's own ceiling in units (new constant vDofLensModel2.x = SplatMaxCoC * 0.5 / U, floored
   at the gather cap so a low splat cap cannot starve the gather). DofPS applies the reach cap
   itself, on every copy of a CoC the kernel derives something from - near reach, far reach, and
   each tap's coverage and density - while the tap's raw alpha stays physical, so what the
   gather writes onward is still the real lens. Second iteration takes the same reach cap;
   composite (beta_far saturates), normalize and the tile min/max pass verified fine larger.

2. The splat pass's constant lane now carries the cap already HALVED: the cvar is documented and
   authored as a DIAMETER while the vertex shader compares it against the quad's half extent, so
   every sprite ceiling was twice what the cvar said. Compared through abs(), so the gather's
   debug sign trick can never leak into a size.

3. Gather taps showed as discrete blobs. 49 taps over a 32 px radius are 9 px apart and every
   pixel samples the source at the same 49 places, so each tap's bilinear footprint reads as a
   separate copy - "several circles trying to form a triangle". Lens mode now runs 11x11 = 121
   taps (g_Taps sized to 121, the count still arriving in vDofParamsFocus1.z, so the stock loop
   reads exactly its own 49), and offsets each tap inside its own cell by a per-pixel amount:
   one interleaved-gradient-noise pair per pixel plus R2 increments per tap, amplitude half the
   tap spacing. The jittered tap is clamped back to the iris polygon's radius at its own angle,
   stored by the CPU in g_Taps[].z - the kernel is never rotated or translated as a whole, so
   the polygon's outline stays exact and only the interior is roughened. TSAA resolves the
   noise. New cvar r_DepthOfFieldLensModelJitter (0..1, default 1); 0 restores the bare grid.
   The tap count and the jitter are logged on the existing [DOF] kernel line.

4. EvalPupilShape's polygon edge width is floored at one native pixel. Blade curvature authors
   0.015 quad-local radius units for a straight blade, which on a 32 px sprite is half a pixel:
   the outline aliased into a dotted line and curvature read as doing nothing. The pixel shader
   knows the sprite's radius in pixels (QuadPos.w), so the floor is 1 / that - and 1 / (that * s)
   for the axial-CA shrunk channel, which is drawn at radius s. A floor, so a curved blade's
   deliberately soft outline is untouched. Both permutations take it; it is our own splat code.

Spec 3.1 / 3.3 / 3.5, README and ConsoleReference updated for the corrected cap semantics and
the new cvar.

